Problem Statement

Create a custom React hook called useTimer that manages a countdown timer.

The hook should expose the following API:

const TOTAL_TIME = 5;

const {
  isRunning,
  start,
  stop,
  seconds,
} = useTimer(TOTAL_TIME);


Using this hook, build a UI with two buttons:

Start – Starts the countdown.
Stop – Stops the countdown and resets it.

When the timer is running, display the remaining seconds on the screen.

When the timer is stopped manually or reaches 0, it should automatically reset back to the initial duration and display:

No Timer Running

Requirements
Create a reusable custom hook named useTimer.
The hook should accept the total countdown duration (in seconds) as an argument.
Initially:
seconds should equal the provided duration.
isRunning should be false.
Clicking Start should:
Begin counting down every second.
Update the remaining time on the screen.
Clicking Stop should:
Stop the countdown immediately.
Reset the timer back to the original duration.
Set isRunning to false.
When the countdown reaches 0:
Stop the timer automatically.
Reset the timer back to the original duration.
Display "No Timer Running".
Clicking Start while the timer is already running should not create multiple intervals.
Clean up timers appropriately to avoid memory leaks.
Function Signature
const {
  isRunning,
  start,
  stop,
  seconds,
} = useTimer(totalTime);

Arguments
totalTime: The initial countdown duration in seconds.
Returns
isRunning: Indicates whether the timer is currently running.
seconds: The remaining time in the countdown.
start: Starts the timer.
stop: Stops the timer and resets it to the initial duration.
Example
Initial State
No Timer Running

[Start] [Stop]

After Clicking Start
5

4

3


...

After Clicking Stop
No Timer Running

After Timer Completes
No Timer Running



SOL:

import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";

const TOTAL_TIME = 5;

function useTimer(totalTime) {
  const [seconds, setSeconds] = useState(totalTime);
  const [isRunning, setIsRunning] = useState(false);

  const intervalRef = useRef(null);

  const start = () => {
    if (isRunning) return;

    setIsRunning(true);
  };

  const stop = () => {
    clearInterval(intervalRef.current);
    intervalRef.current = null;

    setIsRunning(false);
    setSeconds(totalTime);
  };

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isRunning) return;

    intervalRef.current = setInterval(() => {
      setSeconds((prev) => {
        if (prev <= 1) {
          clearInterval(intervalRef.current);
          intervalRef.current = null;
          setIsRunning(false);

          return totalTime;
        }

        return prev - 1;
      });
    }, 1000);

    return () => {
      clearInterval(intervalRef.current);
      intervalRef.current = null;
    };
  }, [isRunning, totalTime]);

  return {
    isRunning,
    start,
    stop,
    seconds,
  };
}

export default function App() {
  const {
    isRunning,
    start,
    stop,
    seconds,
  } = useTimer(TOTAL_TIME);

  return (
    <main>
      <h2>{isRunning ? seconds : "No Timer Running"}</h2>

      <button onClick={start}>Start</button>
      <button onClick={stop}>Stop</button>
    </main>
  );
}

